  "text": "Ikaria EN EN EL FR DE IT ES Ikaria Share Share this page ✕ or copy link Copy 17°C Ikaria 04/10/2026 Humidity 58 % Wind speed 16.7 km/h Ikaria practically dominates the centre of the Aegean Sea, positioned between Mykonos and Samos. Legend has it that this is where Icarus plummeted , having disregarded the counsel of his father, Daedalus, and ventured too close to the sun, causing his waxen wings to melt. Ikaria is a unique land. Sandy beaches, flowing streams, mountains, and verdant slopes coalesce into a majestic topography of rare beauty . The island is renowned for its therapeutic hot springs , celebrated for their curative properties and chemical composition, as well as for the unique lifestyle of its inhabitants . The languid pace , the celebrated panigyria (traditional  festivals), and the intoxicating Ikarian dance combine to create a place with a distinctly individual character. Stunning coastal villages and remote mountain hamlets will captivate you with their natural beauty and unique way of life. In Christos Rachon , one of the island’s most beautiful villages, shops remain open at night, adhering to their own rhythm. Indulge in the coolness and lush vegetation of verdant slopes and picturesque ravines, revel in the pristine sea and sandy beaches, savour fresh fish and robust red wine, join the carefree Ikarians at panigyria (traditional festivals) , and discover the secret to their longevity . Highlights Where Time Flows Differently: The island’s renowned laid-back lifestyle and the secret of its inhabitants’ longevity. A Free Spirit: Famous Ikarian festivals, alternative culture and strong social bonds. Wild Landscapes: Majestic mountains, thermal springs and unspoilt coastlines. + 8 Beaches Category Beaches Happenings Activities By Air Athens International Airport “Eleftherios Venizelos” → Ikaria Airport “Ikaros” (Flight duration: 55 minutes) Thessaloniki Airport “Macedonia” → Ikaria Airport “Ikaros” (Flight duration: 2 hours 15 minutes) Limnos Airport “Hephaestus” → Ikaria Airport “Ikaros” (Flight duration: 55 minutes) Agios Efstratios Thasos Lesvos Limnos August Religious Festivals on Greek Islands Every year on the 15th of August the Orthodox Church celebrates the Dormition of the Virgin Mary, and thousands of pilgrims visit the churches dedicated to Her. After the morning mass, a procession of the Virgin's icon takes place in most villages/ towns, a... Read More Laid Back Islands Each Greek Island has a special atmosphere. Depending on your heart’s desire you can find cosmopolitan or low-key islands; islands known as water & extreme sports destinations; islands preferred by art lovers; islands famous for their intense night life... Read More",
